  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the defiant child visual as a white person who stole their first bike",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the defiant child (girl) as the subject of the text 'when you are white and stole your first bike'. The meme uses the girl's defiant posture and expression as an analogical stand-in for 'you' — the user — who is imagined to be a white person committing the act of stealing a bike. The projection is implicit, relying on the deictic 'you' in the text to anchor the user's identification with the visual subject. The user is not explicitly shown in the image but is semiotically projected onto the girl as the embodiment of the described scenario.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
